[E-TYPE-MISMATCH] Error: type mismatch
    ╭─[ reject/implicit-interface-not-searched.sw:15:63 ]
    │
 15 │ theorem use ∀ (xs: List Int): xs.sumBy idI = xs.sumBy idI2 := sumCong xs idI idI2 fnSame
    │                                                               ─────────────┬────────────  
    │                                                                            ╰────────────── expected `List.sumBy [Int] [Int] [Empty] [Total] [Std.Int.instAdd] xs idI = List.sumBy [Int] [Int] [Empty] [Total] [Std.Int.instAdd] xs idI2`, but this has type `List.sumBy [Int] [Int] [Empty] [Total] [?1 xs] xs idI = List.sumBy [Int] [Int] [Empty] [Total] [?1 xs] xs idI2`
    │ 
    │ Note 1: `?1` is the implicit argument `add` of `sumCong`, which wasn't worked out from the other arguments or the expected type. Its type is an interface, but a plain implicit parameter is never searched for an instance: declare it `[auto add: …]` to have the instance found, or give it with `[add := …]`
    │ 
    │ Note 2: the two types differ only in arguments the compiler fills in, shown here in `[brackets]` (an implicit argument, or a proof the definition computes with; proofs it never computes with are interchangeable)
